  "title": "Two new models for text and images",
  "summary": "New text and image models, community speech publishing, structured agent output, and a good deal less guesswork when requests fail.\n\nQwen3.8 Flash was added for text generation with image and video input, reasoning, tools, and a 1M-token context window. MAI Image 2.5 Flash adds text-to-image generation and editing with one reference image.\n\nPublishers can register text-to-speech models through My Models, the Account API, or the CLI. Community text models and endpoint agents now register an exact Chat Completions or Responses URL, making the upstream API choice explicit.\n\nThe Responses API now returns ordered assistant messages and executed MCP calls for managed agents, with corresponding streaming events. Follow-up requests can include completed tool outputs without rerunning them; API documentation now covers the Responses flow.",
